mimizuku
Copyright (c) 2026 hayatree

mimizuku is an independent Rust and CUDA implementation of Whisper inference. It was written to match Hugging Face
Transformers, so parts of it are translations of that code into another language, modified and restructured
(batched decoding, CUDA graphs, own kernels). Those parts derive from:

- Hugging Face Transformers (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers)
  Copyright 2022-2024 The HuggingFace Inc. team; audio_utils.py also by the librosa and torchaudio authors
  Apache License 2.0
  Log-mel features (WhisperFeatureExtractor, mel filter bank), token timestamps from the alignment heads
  (_extract_token_timestamps: normalisation, median filter, dynamic time warping), generation settings.

- Whisper (https://github.com/openai/whisper)
  Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI, MIT License
  Model architecture, byte-level BPE decoding, and the timing method that Transformers follows.

